#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0483 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. THE 82-RULE GENERATOR-WILDCARD POPULATION (Fix #331 finding; owner ruled 2026-08-22 that all 82 are BUCKET 1 - no rule edit - with a sample of fixtures owed by the closing lane; authored by Fix #340). These rules never carried the injected var_exists guard in rules/ (NonEmptyGuardInliner.isGeneratorWildcard excludes wildcard names), but WildcardExpander re-ran installNativeExpr on the EXPANDED rule, where the arm wrapped the now-concrete leaf - so before Fix #330 an absent primary column silenced them at runtime. With the arm retired the expanded leaf is a bare empty(X): absent = all-missing, TRUE on every row. BCHGCA1N is declared and populated on row 1 while the primary BCHGCAT1 COLUMN is absent entirely; the y=1 tuple is raised off BCHGCA1N and BCHGCAT1 is synthesised absent, so empty(BCHGCAT1) is TRUE and row 1 fires. Row 2 leaves BCHGCA1N blank and stays silent. If this goes silent, the post-expansion guard is back -- escalate."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID    type=Char
col USUBJID    type=Char
col PARAMCD    type=Char
col BCHGCA1N   type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | 2
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | GLUC |
